cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "SGC - Two Horizons: kernel-checked theorems on coarse-graining defects, fluid computation, and regularity budgets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shroyer
    given-names: Jason
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JasonShroyer/sgc-lean"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - Markov generators
  - lumpability
  - Bakry-Emery curvature
  - undecidability
  - Beale-Kato-Majda
  - Navier-Stokes
  - fluid computation
abstract: >-
  Curated Lean 4 formalization: the Kernel Horizon theorem (finite-time closure error
  linear in the lumpability defect), explicit defect-horizon bounds, descent of
  Bakry-Emery curvature bounds along exactly lumpable quotients, Pi^0_1-hardness of a
  global curvature bound via a compiler against Mathlib's Turing machines, exact
  renormalization transparency of Moore's shift, a discrete fluid dictionary, and an
  abstract Beale-Kato-Majda-type budget continuation theorem (L0). All headline theorems
  have kernel closure {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}.
